{"id":"nNyXHtlb","type":"quiz","title":"Stage 1: 2020 AR/VR Africa Hackathon Registration","settings":{"language":"en","progress_bar":"percentage","meta":{"allow_indexing":true,"description":"The 2020 AR/VR Africa Hackathon! Register for Stage 1 and join an Africa community of AR/VR professionals and enthusiasts, access learning resources and tackle online challenges.","image":{"href":"https://images.typeform.com/images/i5kCXpM4Zbgu"}},"hide_navigation":false,"is_public":true,"is_trial":false,"show_progress_bar":false,"show_typeform_branding":true,"are_uploads_public":false,"show_time_to_complete":false,"show_number_of_submissions":false,"show_cookie_consent":false,"show_question_number":true,"hide_required_indicator":false,"show_key_hint_on_choices":true,"autosave_progress":true,"free_form_navigation":false,"use_lead_qualification":false,"pro_subdomain_enabled":false,"email_consent_notifications_config":{"send_email_copy":true},"auto_translate":true,"partial_responses_to_all_integrations":false,"webmcp_enabled":false,"webmcp_submit_hitl_enabled":true},"thankyou_screens":[{"id":"DefaultTyScreen","ref":"default_tys","title":"Thanks for completing this typeform\nNow *create your own* \u2014 it's free, easy, & beautiful","type":"thankyou_screen","properties":{"show_button":true,"share_icons":false,"button_mode":"default_redirect","button_text":"Create a *typeform*"},"attachment":{"type":"image","href":"https://public-assets.typeform.com/public/admin/2dpnUBBkz2VN.gif"}}],"welcome_screens":[{"id":"VRiAHHdrX6NN","ref":"ae1ca8c2862c9a57","title":"*AR/VR Africa Hackathon 2020* ","properties":{"show_button":true,"button_text":"Register now","description":"Preview from July 20th, 2020"},"attachment":{"type":"image","href":"https://images.typeform.com/images/UNT9r6QxDXAC"}}],"fields":[{"id":"0Cf0TuvYq5KF","title":"*The 2020 AR/VR Africa Hackathon! - by Imisi 3D*\nCalling all who love creativity, innovation and learning in Africa! The AR/VR Hackathon is an opportunity to learn about Augmented and Virtual Reality and other immersive technologies, meet new people, and get hands-on experience with AR/VR design and development.\n\n*What is an AR/VR hackathon?*\nA hackathon is a fun, fast-paced, strenuous, yet highly rewarding event where developers/coders, designers, strategists, and enthusiasts come together to work on project ideas and win prizes. \nThe AR/VR hackathon will start as soon as applications open and focus on the rapidly evolving immersive technologies of Augmented and Virtual Reality. It isn\u2019t just about technology. It\u2019s also about learning, design, creation, and problem-solving. If you have an interest in art, graphics, 3D modelling, film, education, sound design, game design, or business, you will enjoy the AR/VR hackathon.\n\n*How will the AR/VR hackathon be held?*\nIn response to the COVID-19 pandemic, we have reviewed the structure of the AR/VR hackathon and created a two-stage event with online and offline components.\nThe online component (Stage 1) will run from the 20th of July 2020. While the offline finale (Stage 2) will take place from the 4th to the 6th of December 2020.\n\n*Who should register?*\nEveryone! Software developers, game programmers, makers, UI/UX designers, artists, animators, storytellers, enthusiasts, professionals, students, and all that want to spend time creating solutions with augmented and virtual reality, and other immersive technologies, and are resident in an African country.\nAfter you register, you will be admitted onto the Discord platform and your online learning will begin. Remember, anyone can go to a hackathon, regardless of their level of expertise.\n\n*How Do I Register For The Hackathon?*\nPlease fill out this form with all of your information. You can also join *the AR/VR Africa Hackathon Facebook group to find team members* for the hackathon. \n\n*I Registered! Does This Guarantee Me A Spot In The Hack?*\nYes. Registration opens on July 20th.\nThe hackathon starts with access to learning resources on our Discord server, and everyone will have access once they have applied. The hackathon begins from the date of registration and runs through the 6th of December 2020.\nThere will be a 2-day Finale, carried out as an offline event in our partner countries. Access to the 2 Day Finale will require a team, and depend on capacity.\n\n*What Type Of Things Should We Build?*\nThere are five verticals for the hackathon - Education; Healthcare including Covid-19 responses; Tourism; Gaming; and Climate. Give your imagination free reign, and conceptualise ways in which we can create solutions in these 5 sectors for African communities.\n\n*What Language Or Platform Can I Use?*\nThe choice is yours! As long as you are confident that you can come up with a working augmented, mixed or virtual reality experience by the end of the hackathon, we are fine.\n\n*Who Owns The Code After We're Done?*\nYou do! We encourage you to open source your code, expand on it, etc. This is a great opportunity to make use of advice from industry experts! However, if you participate in an *Online or Corporate Challenge*, you must abide by the requirements of the sponsoring organisation. All challenge solutions will need to be hosted in GitHub repositories.\n\n*Do I Have To Be On A Team? What If I Don\u2019t Have One?*\nNo, you don't have to be on a team, accessing our Discord server is done individually. While there will be team tasks, general exercises and challenges, your online learning will be at your own pace. You can join the community with your team members, but each team member must complete their own application form. If you do not have a team, you can find team members among the Discord community.\n\nOnce again, all members of your team MUST register individually for the opportunity to attend\\*\n\n*What Should I Bring?*\nNothing! Stage 1 of the hackathon is online. You should bring your A game, great ideas, and have access to a laptop, power, internet, and any augmented and/or virtual reality equipment available.","ref":"ea4d039161dd4ebe","properties":{"button_text":"Continue","hide_marks":false},"type":"statement"},{"id":"Tq2KVRaRkdCP","title":"Thanks for your interest in registering.\nPlease tell us your city.","ref":"9b327f40-5152-47a3-b158-f0b6dc470c5d","properties":{},"validations":{"required":true},"type":"short_text"},{"id":"9pSqCXAdwLjF","title":"Please tell us your country of residence.","ref":"c63590f2-40c1-4de6-8047-bce87b5afd96","properties":{},"validations":{"required":true},"type":"short_text"},{"id":"sjBLq4fkxxyI","title":"Have you joined the AR/VR Africa Facebook Group (https://www.facebook.com/groups/1090243094392331/)?","ref":"3d4e1745-a3fa-41a0-a4f6-2a536c7ff636","properties":{"randomize":false,"allow_multiple_selection":false,"allow_other_choice":false,"vertical_alignment":true,"choices":[{"id":"Vtw0S5w1k4RF","ref":"9d39726a-e1b0-4fba-a3ac-9495acc01eca","label":"Yes (continue with the application form)"},{"id":"3zOxMMkD9Tr8","ref":"91bac25f-49bd-4ac9-ac1b-a5b0521cb108","label":"No (join group now)"}]},"validations":{"required":true},"type":"multiple_choice"},{"id":"j5J3qqNPGSyU","title":"What's your *first name*?","ref":"6fcc4888138ecae4","properties":{},"validations":{"required":true},"type":"short_text","attachment":{"type":"image","href":"https://images.typeform.com/images/9T4uH8HuyaH7"}},{"id":"UDIAvfJcUuuU","title":"What's your* last name*?","ref":"eda8a91d0a4cd181","properties":{},"validations":{"required":true},"type":"short_text","attachment":{"type":"image","href":"https://images.typeform.com/images/ND4BUAiEhZ7V"}},{"id":"o5HzSHRvENI0","title":"You are...","ref":"d7b8f304-a3eb-4d34-8fc9-94e2cba0d54d","properties":{"randomize":false,"allow_multiple_selection":false,"allow_other_choice":true,"vertical_alignment":true,"choices":[{"id":"YDkRMjdrbFub","ref":"06efd7cf-03e9-47a3-8912-b54a59c9c4a0","label":"Female"},{"id":"0jMf5uHWLAt9","ref":"31b2164a-3b14-445b-8201-5a3beefda811","label":"Male"},{"id